WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.760
Thumbs up means...

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.600
well, thumbs up, right?

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.000
But it's not always been that way.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.880
In the Roman era, a thumbs up
meant death for a gladiator.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.200
If the gladiator was to be spared,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.520
the referee would press the thumb
to the top of the fist.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.440
If he flicked it up, it was bad news.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.920
There's a common misconception that
a thumbs down meant death back then.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.440
It's thought to have stemmed from
this painting by Jean-Léon Gérôme

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.160
in 1872,

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.200
which shows a colosseum crowd
with arms outstretched

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.360
and thumbs pointing to the ground.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.360
He got it wrong.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.440
It's though the positive meaning
of thumbs up

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.840
started with English archers
in the Middle Ages.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.160
A fist with thumb up measured the
correct brace height of the longbow,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.000
so the gesture came to mean
"All is well. Ready for battle."

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.600
Another origin of the gesture comes
from merchants in Medieval times.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.320
They would seal a deal

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.880
by licking their thumbs
and pressing them together,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.720
so a thumbs up came to mean
"done deal".

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.320
Allied fighter pilots
in World War Two

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.520
used the gesture to indicate
"chocks away"

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.280
when they were ready for take-off,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.000
and it's thought that American GIs
spread the gesture throughout Europe.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.880
Even today, Italians call it...

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.200
Hitchhikers around the world hope to
"thumb a lift" from passing traffic,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.920
but watch out in Greece, Sardinia
and the Middle East,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.160
where a thumbs up sign is an insult

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.720
and is more likely to get you
into trouble than the next town.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.760
When a scuba diver gives a thumbs up,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.000
it means it's time to swim
back to the surface.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.480
This signal has been known
to confuse beginners.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.480
A wiggled thumbs up means the
number 10 in American sign language,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.880
while a flat palm under a thumbs up
is the sign for "help."

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.360
In the 1990s, influential US
movie reviewers Siskal and Ebert,

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.080
used a thumbs up or thumbs down
rating system on their TV show.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.440
They even trademarked
the phrase "two thumbs up".

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.600
Now, thumbs up and thumbs down signs
are everywhere on the internet.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.840
Hoping for your approval.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.080
Or otherwise.

